          "id": "4db9cee01093c58bb9a0d384c9315a5033d2aa13",
          "message": "test(replication): use RETRIES/RETRY_DELAY constants and add clarifying comments (#5400)\n\n## What\n\nSmall readability cleanup in `tests/tests/replication.rs`, ported from\nthe `paradedb-enterprise` fork to reduce drift between the two. **No\nbehavior change.**\n\n### 1. Use the existing `RETRIES` / `RETRY_DELAY` constants\n\nThe file already defines:\n```rust\nconst RETRIES: u32 = 60;\nconst RETRY_DELAY: u64 = 1000; // measured in milliseconds\n```\nand uses them in `test_logical_replication`, but\n`test_physical_streaming_replication` and\n`test_wal_streaming_replication_with_pg_search` still passed the raw\n`60, 1000` literals to `fetch_retry`. This swaps those over so the retry\ntuning is consistent and named everywhere.\n\n### 2. A few clarifying comments in\n`test_wal_streaming_replication_with_pg_search`\n\nAdded comments above code that was previously uncommented (the insert\nstep, the `--pgdata` permissions requirement — which already has the\nidentical comment in `test_ephemeral_postgres_with_pg_basebackup` — and\nthe standby pg_search preload).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Values are identical (`RETRIES == 60`, `RETRY_DELAY == 1000`), so\nretry behavior is unchanged.\n- `cargo fmt --check` is clean (rustfmt wrapped a few of the now-longer\n`fetch_retry` calls).\n- Scope is limited to comments + constant substitution; no test logic\nchanged.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-23T16:14:18-04:00",
