          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2c20680a80ff2a66155f76bd1fe0f83c9cb2ffe3",
          "message": "fix: Reset token position per document in unicode_words tokenizer (#5368)\n\nThe `unicode_words` tokenizer (the default) never reset its `Token`\nposition counter in `token_stream()`. tantivy reuses one tokenizer\ninstance across every document in a segment, and the `Token` lives on\nthe tokenizer, so the position counter accumulated across all documents\ninstead of restarting at 0 per document.\n\nWithin a document positions stay consecutive, so query results\n(including phrase/proximity) remain correct, but the absolute position\nvalues grow into the hundreds of millions. Tantivy bitpacks position\ndeltas in fixed blocks at the width of the largest value, and the\nper-document first position is that value, so leaked positions inflate\nthe positions index substantially (~2.7x measured on a 28.7M-row corpus)\nand risk a u32 overflow on very large segments.\n\nFix: call `self.token.reset()` at the top of `token_stream()`, matching\ntantivy's built-in `SimpleTokenizer`/`WhitespaceTokenizer`. Add a\nregression test that reuses one tokenizer instance across two documents\nand asserts positions restart at 0.\n\nNote: `lindera` reuses the token too but overwrites position with an\nabsolute per-call value; `cjk`/`icu`/`edge_ngram`/`ngram` build a fresh\ntoken per stream. Only unicode_words was affected.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-30T09:12:36-07:00",
