          "id": "37562e7a45a1bd8ad5e95960dc7dd0c8799e1fab",
          "message": "refactor(mpp): launched MPP workers via the parallel_worker builder. (#5363)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #5061\n\n## What\n\nLaunches the MPP producer workers through `parallel_worker::builder`,\nwith the leader picking the count, instead of tricking PG into a\n`Gather` over a partial path.\n\n## Why\n\n#5061: when PG launches fewer workers than the mesh expects, the\nunfilled `shm_mq` slots never detach, the cooperative pull never sees\nthem done, and the leader hangs. With the leader owning the launch, a\nshort launch becomes a clean serial fallback. The node also stays serial\nto PG, so #5152's `add_upper_path` / `create_gather_path` trick drops\nout.\n\n## How\n\n`mpp/launch.rs` carries the MPP DSM as builder `ParallelState` entries:\nthe ring-mesh blob, the `ParallelScanState` blob, the\npartitioning-source index, and a go flag. The leader populates the scan\nstate and builds the dispatch before launch, runs `leader_setup` only\nafter the full producer set is up, then releases the workers through the\ngo flag. Workers rebuild their `MppWorkerInputs` from those entries and\nrun `run_mpp_worker`.\n\n`shutdown_custom_scan` drops the gather stream, which frees\n`LIMIT`-blocked producers through the leader detach, then `recv()`s the\nworkers before draining metrics, so `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` keeps the\nper-worker `output_rows`. The worker-via-plan-tree path is gone:\n`mpp/host.rs`, the per-scan host impls, the `MppExecState::Worker`\nvariant, and the DSM header helpers. The DSM callbacks now serve only\nthe regular parallel join.\n\nDepends on paradedb/datafusion-distributed#24; the early-terminated\nbuilder teardown relies on it.\n\n## Tests\n\nExisting test with the updated outputs for regression tests.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
