          "id": "f9f81c7ae732ca35fd7019e9a499bd435a00e213",
          "message": "perf: replace BinaryHeap with Vec + QuickSelect in SegmentedTopKExec (#5380)\n\n## What\n\nReplaces the per-segment bounded `BinaryHeap` in `SegmentedTopKExec`\nwith a `Vec` buffer partitioned via `select_nth_unstable` (QuickSelect).\n\nEach per-segment buffer grows up to `2 * K` rows. When it reaches `2 *\nK`, a single QuickSelect pass partitions it around the K-th best row\n(index `k - 1`): that row is recorded as the segment cutoff, and the\nbuffer is truncated back to its K best rows. This mirrors Tantivy's\n`TopNComputer`.\n\n## Why\n\nThis is **prework split out of #4739** at @stuhood's request, so the\nvisibility-filtering change can land on top of a smaller, focused\nrefactor:\n\n> Sorry for the delayed feedback, but: would you mind splitting the swap\nto `select_nth_unstable` into a separate prework PR? That should help us\nland the whole thing more quickly.\n\nSwapping the heap for QuickSelect replaces the `O(log K)` push/pop\nperformed on every ingested row with `O(1)` amortized buffering plus one\n`O(buffer)` selection at each `2 * K` boundary.\n\n## How\n\n- `segment_heaps: HashMap<_, BinaryHeap<OwnedRow>>` is replaced by\n`segment_bufs: HashMap<_, Vec<OwnedRow>>` plus `segment_cutoffs:\nHashMap<_, OwnedRow>` (the K-th best row after the most recent\nQuickSelect).\n- `collect_batch` pre-filters rows already worse than a segment's\ncutoff, buffers the rest, and runs the inline QuickSelect when a buffer\nhits `2 * K`.\n- `build_survivors`, `publish_global_threshold`, and `maybe_compact`\nread the cutoff from `segment_cutoffs` instead of peeking the heap root.\n- The legacy `update_cutoff_heap` helper and the `BinaryHeap` import are\nremoved.\n\n## Behavior\n\nNo observable change in results: the same top-K rows survive per\nsegment, and the same global threshold is pushed down for dynamic-filter\npruning (now published after a segment's first QuickSelect rather than\nas soon as it reaches K rows).\n\n## Tests\n\nNo expected-output changes were needed. Verified locally on PG18:\n\n- `cargo fmt -- --check` and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --\n-D warnings` clean\n- `pg_test_segmented_topk_exec` proptest passes (multi-segment random\nsubsets, exact top-K assertion)\n- `pg_regress` suites pass with no `.out` diffs: `join_*` (45), `topk_*`\n(12), `order_by_*` (5), `term_set_*` (5), including `segmented_topk`,\n`join_sort_merge`, and `topk_dynamic_filter`",
